    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44281" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔκομος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόμη</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lovely-haired</i>, of goddesses and noble ladies, 
				Ep.
			 and Lyr. form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠΰκομος</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.36
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				241
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				6.91
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>P.</u>
				5.45
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σελήνη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epimenid.
					2
				</span></i>
			: in Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				29
			</span></i>; <i>well-fleeced</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔκομα μῆλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.363.20
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Mel.
			</span></i>); <i>with goodly foliage</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δένδρεσιν ἠϋκόμοισιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Emp.
					127.2
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Alex.Aphr.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				2.51
			</span></i>.</div>
